The material questions, which are required to be gone into for grant of the relief of specific performance, are First, whether there exists a valid and concluded contract between the parties for sale/purchase of the suit property;
Second, whether the plaintiff has been ready and willing to perform his part of contract and whether he is still ready and willing to perform his part as mentioned in the contract;
Third, whether the plaintiff has, in fact, performed his part of the contract and, if so,
how and to what extent and in what manner he has performed and whether such performance was in conformity with the terms of the contract;
Fourth, whether it will be equitable to grant the relief of specific performance to the plaintiff against the defendant in relation to suit property or it will cause any kind of hardship to the defendant and, if so, how and in what manner and the extent if such relief is eventually granted to the plaintiff; and Judgment Page No. 68 of 114 dated 09.05.2025 M DJ No. 61199/2015 (Main Suit) CNR No. : DLCT01-004795-2015 Durga Devi Vs Kirpa Ram and CS DJ No. 11871/2016 (Connected Suit) CNR No.
